INT. A SECRET WORKSHOP - DAY

Dingy, with a ratty dressmaker’s dummy and a broken sewing machine powered by foot. Light filters through cracked shutters.

Rats gnaw a piece of moldy bread. A cockroach runs across pile of dirty clothes.

Through bars in the window, a hummingbird enters the workshop. This is BOBBIN.

The bird buzzes around with urgency, from corner to corner. It stops.

Bobbin flies to the pile of laundry, pecks the cockroach and sends it scurrying.

It finds the top of the head of a woman and pecks it. There’s a groan. Bobbin pecks it again.

The woman belonging to the head rolls over, pair of scissors held in her hand like a weapon. Her eyes are wide in terror.

Freeze on black and white of this image.

OVERLOCK (V.O.)
My name is Overlock Stitch. I’m wanted for a capital offense.

She sits up, her face dirty, hair a mess. Bobbin flies around her head.

Flashback:

INT. SECRET WORKSHOP - DAY

There’s a pounding on the door.

Bobbin buzzes to and fro, frantic.

Overlock creeps over to the door. She eases it open.

Standing on the other side, chewing a matchstick, is Flame - the little match girl.

They stare at each other in silence.

FLAME
It true?

OVERLOCK
Is what true?

FLAME
About your dad?

OVERLOCK
Yeah.

FLAME
And the other thing.

Overlock bites her lip. Nods.

Flame chews the match. Nods.

OVERLOCK
I’m going to break into the Emperor’s Palace, break out my father and steal all his gold.

Flame laughs.

FLAME
Cool.
